bof-lyp	hello world\nsecond line\nthird\n	0	-	-	-	lyp	Emacs leaves the point one character past the text it yanked, when the kill came from a line selection. Traced rather than guessed: `yank` is entered at 13 and returns at 25, correctly, and something in Meow's post-command path then moves point to 26. Identical under whole-macro replay, so it is Meow's behaviour and not a harness artifact -- but the mechanism is unidentified, and reproducing an offset nobody can explain is the cargo-culting ADR-0002 exists to prevent. ADR-0006 puts a stray point offset outside what Fidelity binds.
